Wenmang — third-party data notices
==================================

The application code in this repository is original work. Two third-party
data sets are used, and neither is redistributed from this repository: both
are fetched at runtime or consulted at build time. They are named here because
attribution is owed regardless of how the data reaches a user.


1. Character stroke data — Make Me a Hanzi
------------------------------------------
Stroke outlines, medians and stroke order are served to the browser at runtime
from the `hanzi-writer-data` package (https://github.com/chanind/hanzi-writer).
That data comes from Make Me a Hanzi (https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi),
which derives it from the Arphic PL fonts:

    "AR PL Mingti2L Big5" and "AR PL KaitiM Big5" (BIG-5)
    "AR PL SungtiL GB" and "AR PL KaitiM GB" (GB)

    Copyright (C) 1999 Arphic Technology Co., Ltd.

Used under the Arphic Public License. The full licence text ships with the
data package as ARPHICPL.TXT and is reproduced at:
https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi/blob/master/ARPHICPL.TXT

Note for maintainers: the Arphic Public License attaches obligations to
*distributing* the font data, and additional obligations to distributing a
*modified* copy — and it counts "adding/deleting some characters in/from glyph
table" as modification. This project therefore does not vendor a trimmed subset
of the data. If that ever changes, section 2 of the licence requires the
modification to be documented and made freely available under the same terms.
See source/strokes.js, which is the only module that touches this data.


2. Radical and stroke-count data — Unicode Han Database (Unihan)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The `radical`, `residual` and `strokes` fields in source/character-data.js are
generated from the kRSUnicode and kTotalStrokes fields of the Unihan database.

    Copyright (C) 1991-present Unicode, Inc.

Used under the Unicode License. Unihan is not vendored here; it is downloaded
on demand by tools/build-characters.mjs, which regenerates the table.


